# SAFETY GATE for the Galaxy Tab S7's CS35L41 speaker amps
# (docs/phase3-audio-scoping.md, "Stage 3/4 design", hard rules).
#
# Opening a playback stream powers the amps through DAPM regardless of any
# mixer setting, and each amp's "PCM Source" resets to ASP - speaker
# protection bypassed. Until protection firmware + calibration are verified
# on all four amps, no user process (PipeWire/WirePlumber, KDE) may open the
# sound devices: root-only 0600, and no uaccess ACL. Must sort before
# 73-seat-late.rules, which applies uaccess.
#
# Remove this file only once the verified-safe setup (UCM with PCM Source =
# DSP and the gain ceilings) is in place.
SUBSYSTEM=="sound", KERNEL=="pcmC*|controlC*|comprC*|hwC*", TAG-="uaccess", OWNER="root", GROUP="root", MODE="0600"
